==Latin==
[[Image:France map with Loire highlighted.jpg|thumb|350px|''<b>Tabula</b> Franciae cum flumine Ligere insignata''<sup> {{w|Liger|lang=la|W}}</sup><br><u>Map</u> of France with river Loire]]

===Etymology===
The origin is {{unk.|la|title=uncertain}}. Perhaps from {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{recons|th₂-dʰlo-|lang=ine-pro}}, from {{recons|teh₂-||to stand|lang=ine-pro}} (a variety of {{recons|steh₂-|lang=ine-pro|title=}} without [[s-mobile]], whence also Latin {{term|sto|stō, stāre|to stand|lang=la}}) + {{recons|-dʰlo-||instrumental suffix|lang=ine-pro}}. The original meaning would then be “that which stands”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈta.bu.la/|lang=la}}
* {{audio|la-cls-tabula.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|tabula|tabulae|tabulae|f|first}}

# [[tablet]], sometimes a tablet covered with [[wax]] for [[writing]]
# [[board]] or [[plank]]
# {{context|by extension|lang=la}} [[map]], [[painting]], [[document]] or other item put onto a tablet

